{
 "version": 1,
 "assumptions": [
  "managed::authenticate is the only reader of the Authorization header and returns a Principal only for a key whose SHA-256 hash maps to a live key of an active place (cache, fresh lookup, or a stale cached entry while the server is unreachable); it refuses with outside_network exactly when the canonical peer IP lies in an approved range of an org other than the key's org (C30, C77).",
  "policy::effective::decide decides with the EffectivePolicy carried by the Principal it is given (applying exceptions, then calling today's unchanged policy::evaluate) and reads no App-global policy input in managed mode.",
  "probation_policy::check_edit accepts a proposed layer only when every loosening or grant it adds or widens compared with the stored layer is allowed by the matching switch of the layer above (C8, C11, C45); unchanged kept settings pass and stay not in effect through resolve (C47).",
  "The server writes the layer, its change_log row and its audit_log row in one PostgreSQL transaction; a failed transaction writes none of them.",
  "Firewall concurrency on the key cache is modelled as atomic per-entry replacement; interleavings across requests are not modelled. A lookup or layers answer read at a change-log revision older than the entry's last invalidation is dropped, not cached (held by T-sync-late-answer-dropped).",
  "Each outcome's unknown guard facts are nondeterministic: the model checks that every outcome is routed, not which real inputs select it.",
  "The server assigns change_log revisions in commit order (one locked counter row), so a firewall cursor never passes an uncommitted change; a changed key's entry is removed, a changed layer is refetched and every interned policy containing it rebuilt with no key lookup, and a changed place (suspension, deletion) expires every cached entry whose chain contains it.",
  "Every portal policy-edit route first resolves the target place with tenancy::authorized_place, which answers 404 for a place outside the actor's places before any policy is loaded (C1, T9); the policy-edit flow starts after that call (held by T-tenant-isolation).",
  "http::admit answers 503 NOT_READY before calling authenticate while no snapshot is loaded and no sync is applied, or when the peer address is missing; the managed-request flow starts after that gate (held by T-auth-not-ready-503)."
 ],
